From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wsi: Trace only the first acquires unless asked.

The 0032 acquire trace logged every acquire after the 1024th, about 8 lines
per frame for the rest of a session (19,592 lines in WON Half-Life on 01.12,
which was choppy). Keep the first eight; ORBIS_WSI_TRACE_LATE_ACQUIRE=1
restores the late trace.
---
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
@@ -2297,7 +2297,15 @@
 
 #ifdef HAVE_ORBIS_PLATFORM
    const int32_t trace = p_atomic_inc_return(&orbis_acquire_stage_count);
-   const bool trace_this = trace <= 8 || trace >= 1024;
+   /* ⚠ THE FIRST EIGHT ONLY, unless asked. Tracing every acquire after the 1024th wrote ~8 log lines per
+    * frame for the rest of a session (19,592 lines in a few minutes of WON Half-Life, 01.12) - a stall
+    * hunt's instrument left running in every title. ORBIS_WSI_TRACE_LATE_ACQUIRE=1 brings it back. */
+   static int trace_late = -1;
+   if (trace_late < 0) {
+      const char *late = getenv("ORBIS_WSI_TRACE_LATE_ACQUIRE");
+      trace_late = late != NULL && late[0] != '\0' && late[0] != '0';
+   }
+   const bool trace_this = trace <= 8 || (trace_late && trace >= 1024);
    if (trace_this)
       mesa_logi("wsi/orbis: 0032 acquire #%d common entry timeout=%llu sem=%u fence=%u",
                 trace, (unsigned long long)pAcquireInfo->timeout,
